    "classification": "release-blocking-scope-and-consent-mismatch",
    "severity": "critical-for-exact-origin-targets",
    "summary": "Chrome treats an extension origin-list browsing-data request as selected-top-level-site cleanup for partitioned storage. The current review does not disclose that third-party LocalStorage, IndexedDB, Cache Storage, file-system data, service workers, and related data partitioned beneath the selected site can be removed. Chrome's schemeful-site partition key also ignores ports, so this browser-level operation cannot preserve SiteWipe's reviewed exact-origin port boundary for localhost and IP targets.",
    "whyTheCookieRemained": "Chrome handles cookies through a separate host-based path. The out-of-domain chips.localhost partitioned cookie remained outside the reviewed example.com cookie scope.",
    "whySessionStorageIsSupportingOnly": "Closing the matching top-level tab also destroys its browsing context. The persistent LocalStorage and IndexedDB results are the decisive browser-semantic evidence.",
    "productionLocation": "src/background/origin-storage.js#removeOriginScopedStorage",
    "releaseBlocker": true
  },
